                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <locus from="4r" to="40r"/>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red (different tones of red)</seg>
                        <date notBefore="1700" notAfter="1899">eighteenth or nineteenth
                           century</date>
                        <seg type="script">Careful but somewhat irregular hand. The scribe wrote the
                           last three lines of <ref target="#ms_i3"/> in small script in order to
                           complete the section on the same folio <locus target="#33v"/>. Characters
                           are occasionally set at wide intervals to fill the line at the end of a
                           text (e g. <locus target="#34v #35r"/>).</seg>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Two initial lines, and occasionally two more lines
                           further down, in the incipit of all texts; first word of each stanza of
                              <ref target="#ms_i1 #ms_i3 #ms_i8"/>; holy names; the name of the
                           apparent owner <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS13232EhetaMar">ʾƎḫǝta Māryām</persName>; elements
                           of the punctuation marks, text dividers, and numerals.</seg>
                        <list type="abbreviations">
                           <item>
                              <abbr>መ፡</abbr> for <expan>መለኮት፡</expan> (<ref target="#ms_i8"/>)
                           </item>
                        </list>
                     </handNote>

                     <handNote xml:id="h2" script="Ethiopic" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/MNC010#a1">
                        <locus from="2r" to="2v"/>
                        <seg type="ink">Black</seg>
                        <desc>Mediocre. Broad script with hairlines.</desc>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>

                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1" corresp="#h2">
                           <locus from="2r" to="2v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">
                              <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2701Dawit">Excerpt from the Psalter</title> The excerpt
                              comprises <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2701Dawit.118.2-14">Ps
                                 118,2–14</ref>. </desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">
                              <locus target="#2r"/>
                              <seg part="I">
                                 <lb n="1"/>ብፁዓን፡ እለ፡ የኀሡ፡ ስምዖ። <lb n="2"/>ወበኵሉ፡ ልቦሙ፡ የኃሥዎ። <lb n="3"/>እለሰ፡ ይገብሩ፡ ዓመፃ፡ ፍኖተ፡ ዚአሁ፡ ኢሖሩ። <lb n="4"/>እንተ፡ አዘዝከ፡
                                 ይዕቀቡ፡ ትእዛዘከ፡ ፈድፋደ።</seg>
                           </q>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <desc> Scribal corrections occur interlineally (e.g. <locus target="#4r #5v #7v"/>), occasionally over erasures (e.g. <locus target="#17r"/>. Erroneous characters or words are encircled with a
                              red line, or with dots in red and black (e.g. <locus target="#8r  #18r #34v"/>).</desc>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="e2">
                           <desc> The name of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS13357Batha"><roleName type="title">Wayzaro</roleName> Batḫā</persName> is written in pencil in the
                              lower margin of <locus target="#2r"/>, the name of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS13357Batha"><roleName type="title">Wayzaro</roleName>
                                 Ḍaḥaytu</persName> on <locus target="#3v"/>.</desc>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="e3">
                           <desc> Writing exercises in different hands were executed on <locus target="#1r #2v #3r #3v #40v"/>, of the orders of the labiovelar
                              characters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ኰ</foreign>, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ጐ</foreign>, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ቈ</foreign>,
                              and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ኰ</foreign> on <locus target="#1r"/>.
                              Rough sketch of an ornamental band in pen on <locus target="#1v #41r"/>.</desc>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="e4">
                           <desc> A sticker of the monastic library with the signature ‘Ms 38’ is
                              glued onto the inner side of the front board. The signature Et III is
                              written in pencil in the upper margin of <locus target="#1r"/>. The
                              inventory number 50435 is written in pencil on <locus target="#40r"/>.</desc>
                        </item>
                     </list>
                  </additions>

                  <bindingDesc>
                     
                     <binding contemporary="false" xml:id="binding">
                        <decoNote xml:id="b1">Two<material key="wood">wooden</material> boards
                           covered with tooled dark reddish-brown <material key="leather"/>, textile
                           inlays.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b2" type="bindingMaterial">
                           <material key="wood"/>
                           <material key="leather"/>
                           <material key="textile"/>
                        </decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b3" type="Cover" color="reddish-brown">Skilled
                           blind-tooling decoration on the boards: two frames with a cross inside,
                           the turn-ins and the edges are carefully tooled with lines forming
                           crosses and double circles.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b4" type="SewingStations">6 (The original binding showed
                           only two sewing stations. The Ms received additional four sewing stations
                           during the restoration process (<ref target="#condition"/>).</decoNote>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
               </physDesc>

               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate notBefore="1700" notAfter="1899" evidence="lettering"/> The earliest
                     date of production—taking into account the handwriting—can be set to the
                     eighteenth century. The name of <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS13232EhetaMar">ʾƎḫǝta Māryām</persName> is mentioned in a few supplication formulas
                     following the phrase <foreign xml:lang="gez">አመትኪ፡</foreign> ‘your maid’. This
                     person was most probably the owner of the manuscript.</origin>
               </history>

